\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Forth in Thy name, O Lord, I go,
\par My daily labour to pursue,
\par Thee, only Thee, resolved to know
\par In all I think, or speak, or do.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. The task Thy wisdom hath assigned
\par O let me cheerfully fulfil,
\par In all my works Thy presence find,
\par And prove Thy acceptable will.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Thee may I set at my right hand,
\par Whose eyes my inmost substance see,
\par And labour on at Thy command,
\par And offer all my works to Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Give me to bear Thy easy yoke,
\par And every moment watch and pray,
\par And still to things eternal look,
\par And hasten to Thy glorious day:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. For Thee delightfully employ
\par Whate'er Thy bounteous grace hath given,
\par And run my course with even joy,
\par And closely walk with Thee to heaven
\par 
